# Multi-subject — M1b Parallel enumeration (analyzer vs finalizer emit channels)
#
# Companion to m1a. Where m1a asks about a RELATION between two
# agents, m1b asks a PARALLEL ENUMERATION: name the single emit_*
# tool each of analyzer and finalizer uses. IsRelationalLookup
# should be false here (no relation being queried — two independent
# lookups), so the new multi-subject path produces the set-anchored
# explainHypothesis / two enumerate hypotheses WITHOUT the pairwise
# relation hypothesis. That distinguishes this case from m1a and
# tests the non-relation multi-subject branch.
#
# Ground truth (internal/orchestrator/topology.go + internal/tool/
# emit_analysis.go + internal/tool/emit_answer_document.go):
#   - analyzer → emit_analysis (single mandatory emit at analyze stage)
#   - finalizer → emit_answer_document (single mandatory emit at finalize)
#
# EXPECT_SECTIONS requires both agent names. EXPECT_CONTAINS pins
# the two tool names so neither side can be glossed over. A vague
# answer listing "various emit_* tools" fails because it hedges on
# the one-to-one mapping.
ID="m1b"
NAME="parallel enumeration — analyzer and finalizer emit tools"
QUESTION="codrax 的 analyzer agent 和 finalizer agent 分别通过哪一个 emit_* 工具把本 stage 的结构化输出写出去？两个 agent 各列一个工具名。"
EXPECT_CONTAINS="emit_analysis emit_answer_document"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS=".java .py same.tool"
EXPECT_SECTIONS="analyzer finalizer"
